| <span lang="ja">段階</span><span lang="en">Stage</span> | <span lang="ja">確認する内容</span><span lang="en">What is checked</span> | <span lang="ja">次に確認する内容</span><span lang="en">Complementary check</span> |
| --- | --- | --- |
| <span lang="ja">CML解析・正規化</span><span lang="en">CML parsing / normalization</span> | <span lang="ja">文法・型参照・種別・宣言の整合</span><span lang="en">Grammar, type references, kinds, declarations</span> | <span lang="ja">要求の意味との適合</span><span lang="en">Requirement meaning</span> |
| <span lang="ja">型付き実装・コンパイル</span><span lang="en">Typed implementation / compilation</span> | <span lang="ja">入出力・型の合成</span><span lang="en">Inputs, outputs, type composition</span> | <span lang="ja">規則の妥当性と実行結果</span><span lang="en">Rule validity and execution results</span> |
| <span lang="ja">モデルレビュー</span><span lang="en">Model review</span> | <span lang="ja">要求・構造・判断・進行の対応</span><span lang="en">Requirements, structure, decisions, progression</span> | <span lang="ja">実際の接続と失敗時の動作</span><span lang="en">Actual bindings and failure behavior</span> |
| <span lang="ja">実行検証</span><span lang="en">Execution verification</span> | <span lang="ja">正常・境界・例外の実例</span><span lang="en">Normal, boundary and exceptional examples</span> | <span lang="ja">変更した定義と実例の追随</span><span lang="en">Keep definitions and examples aligned</span> |

# Establishing Model Connections with a Small Use Case｜小さなユースケースからモデルの接続を確かめる

<span lang="ja">最初は一つの目的を選び、必要な用語、入出力、EntityとValue、判断規則、Workflowと状態機械の対応をそろえます。参照と表示も同じ目的へ接続し、利用者の操作から結果が返るまでを確認します。図を増やすことより、モデル間で型・意味・状態の対応が保たれていることを確認します。</span><span lang="en">Begin with one goal and connect the necessary terminology, inputs and outputs, Entities and Values, decision rules, Workflow and state machines. Add reading and presentation for the same goal and verify the path from user action to result. The focus is consistency of types, meaning and state across models rather than increasing the number of diagrams.</span>

<span lang="ja">複数のユースケースを扱う中で、共通する概念や規則をドメインへ整理し、各ユースケースを実現する進行はアプリケーション側へ置きます。ユースケースと実現モデルの対応は要求実現の関係です。一方、ドメインに近いモデルを実装・実行の表現へ具体化し、得られた知見をモデルへ戻すモデル・アップ・ダウンは、抽象度をまたぐ作業として区別します。</span><span lang="en">As more use cases are added, shared concepts and rules are organized in the domain, while goal-specific progression remains in the application. Use-case realization links requirements to implementing models. Model up/down is a different activity: moving between domain-level descriptions and implementation or execution representations, and feeding discovered insights back into the model.</span>

# Conclusion｜まとめ

<span lang="ja">CMLによるモデリングでは、用語、構造、規則、振る舞い、参照と表示を分担して記述し、それらの対応を保ちます。型と制約は値の扱いを、ルールは判断を、Workflowと状態機械は進行を定め、生成とTextus/CNCFの実行機構がそれを実装へ結び付けます。この構成は再利用と変更を支え、AIが補完する範囲を明確にするため、モデル駆動開発の仕組みがAI開発のハーネスとしても機能します。</span><span lang="en">CML modeling divides responsibility among terminology, structure, rules, behavior, reading and presentation while preserving their relationships. Types and constraints govern values, rules govern decisions, and Workflows and state machines govern progression; generation and Textus/CNCF connect these definitions to implementation. This structure supports reuse and change and clarifies the scope of AI supplementation, allowing model-driven development to function as an AI development harness.</span>

# Appendix: Sources and Related Guides｜付録：参照資料と関連ガイド

<span lang="ja">本文はCozyの受理済み文法・生成契約、CNCFのRule Engine基盤、SimpleModelingのモデリング方針をもとにしています。以下は内部リポジトリ資料です。最新文法の設計資料には実装予定も含まれるため、一般RULE DSLなどの拡張方針と、受理済みのDatatype・Operation・Workflow契約を区別しています。</span><span lang="en">This guide draws on Cozy’s accepted grammar and generation contracts, CNCF’s Rule Engine foundation and SimpleModeling’s modeling approach. The following are internal repository sources. Latest-grammar design material includes planned work, so extension directions such as the general RULE DSL are distinguished from accepted Datatype, Operation and Workflow contracts.</span>

